equiring_human_adjudication": [\n    "D008: conflicting apparent bed size and relative priority of door orientation versus lighting; inspect images without showing predictions first.",\n    "D007: whether visible door orientation or framing matters more, and whether T1\'s omission of the former matters.",\n    "I004: relative importance of invisible door versus framing, without inferring whether a door exists outside frame.",\n    "I003: whether apparent window proportion or lighting is more salient given the very different viewpoint.",\n    "D012: T0 priority 2 concerns the right-hand furnishing while T1 priority 3 concerns the cabinet; the cropped furnishing\'s identity is uncertain."\n  ],\n  "conclusions_supported_now": [\n    "The generic critic spontaneously names position/layout, orientation, proportions, and material/texture in recorded cases, overlapping the broad kinds in the provisional principle, without per-case human agreement being known.",\n    "The additional principle is associated with changed priorities and sometimes category or severity, often without changing the first category or score. Shared diagnoses, reversals, and conflicts all occur."\n  ],\n  "conclusions_not_supported": [\n    "Improved human alignment, validated universal weights, actual reconstruction improvement from a higher automated score, semantic or 3D correctness, or population-level preference.",\n    "Causal attribution of every difference to the principle rather than session stochasticity, or independent statistical inference from correlated versions and only two new scenes.",\n    "Human labels, T2/T3 training or execution, technical diagnosis, exploration guidance, or student capability learning in this batch."\n  ],\n  "next_steps_after_genuine_human_feedback": [\n    "Obtain separate genuine offline development and independent exports; preserve the frozen T0/T1 predictions and inspect human scores, prioritized defects, pair preferences and disagreements without treating